## 7. Replay Design

### 7.1 Event Kinds

| Kind | What it does | Passes through | Result |
|---|---|---|---|
| **traffic** | Writes one or more packets into the NIDS packet table, unlabelled | NIDS's detector, called immediately (DD-5), then event processing | Security event labelled by NIDS's detector |
| **technique** | Injects a scripted ATT&CK technique for a host (imitating Caldera and Atomic Red Team output) | Event processing only | Security event with a technique, source marked `scripted` |
| **attempt** | An attempted move from one host to another | Graph and containment check | Becomes `success` or `blocked` depending on whether the target is contained |

### 7.2 Scenario File Format

```json
{
  "scenario_id": "golden-path",
  "description": "Recon, credential attack, lateral movement, simulated exfiltration",
  "events": [
    { "seq": 1, "offset_ms": 0,    "kind": "technique", "host": "host-a", "technique_id": "T1046", "note": "network scan" },
    { "seq": 2, "offset_ms": 1500, "kind": "traffic",   "packets": [ { "src_host": "host-a", "dst_host": "host-b", "protocol": "TCP", "dst_port": 22, "size": 800, "flags": "S" } ] },
    { "seq": 3, "offset_ms": 3000, "kind": "technique", "host": "host-a", "technique_id": "T1110", "compromise": true },
    { "seq": 4, "offset_ms": 4500, "kind": "attempt",   "from_host": "host-a", "to_host": "server-b", "pause_for_decision": true }
  ]
}
```

(Values are illustrative; real techniques are chosen in the build guides and checked against the ATT&CK data.)

| Rule | Detail |
|---|---|
| `pause_for_decision` | The replay stops **before** this event and waits for the analyst's decision or a manual resume (PRD FR-ING-9) |
| `compromise: true` | Marks where a host becomes compromised, which triggers a forecast |
| Suspicious traffic | Scripted attack packets use destination ports that NIDS's detector already treats as suspicious, so the real detector flags them (Section 5.1) |
| Time | `offset_ms` is relative to replay start; a speed factor multiplies the pace |
| Determinism | Same file and speed give the same result (P7) |

### 7.3 Demo Network

Six hosts, Proposed. Packet records identify hosts by IP address, so each host has a fixed address in a **host mapping table**.

| Host ID | Role | Zone | Address (Proposed) |
|---|---|---|---|
| `host-a` | User workstation (entry point) | user | 192.168.1.11 |
| `host-b` | User workstation | user | 192.168.1.12 |
| `server-b` | Web server (the golden path's predicted target) | dmz | 192.168.1.20 |
| `file-server` | File server | internal | 192.168.1.30 |
| `db-server` | Database server | internal | 192.168.1.40 |
| `domain-controller` | Domain controller | internal | 192.168.1.50 |

Feasible connections, services and vulnerabilities per host are defined in the GRAPH guide using `attackgraph`'s asset and vulnerability structures.

### 7.4 Input Paths

| Path | Input | Use |
|---|---|---|
| **A. Scripted scenarios** | Scenario files | Default and the golden path |
| **B. PCAP file** | A recorded packet capture file | Could-have. NIDS's own upload only **analyses** the file and returns results; it does **not** store packets (tested). To replay a PCAP, the replay writer would read the file and insert its packets into the NIDS packet table itself |

CICIDS2017 is **not** a replay input. It is used offline only (Section 8.3).

### 7.5 Scenario Generator (for Precog Training)

A seeded script generates many varied attack sequences over the feasible paths, using several attacker "strategy profiles". Count and split are in Section 9.7. The seed is recorded so any run can be reproduced.

### 7.6 Database Housekeeping

| Item | Design |
|---|---|
| Size | The replay writer keeps the packet table small (Proposed: about 500 rows, the same limit NIDS's simulator uses) because each NIDS request reads the whole table |
| Restart | Restarting the replay clears the packet table and resets the add-on state |
| Time | The writer stores scenario time (UTC) in NIDS's timestamp column |

