## 17. Performance and Capacity Design

| Item | Design |
|---|---|
| Scale | 6 hosts, about 500 packet rows at most, 2 to 4 clients |
| Latency budget (PRD NFR-PERF-1, Proposed 3 s) | Writer → NIDS detector called directly → event processing → state version bump → next poll (1 to 2 seconds). Detection on a few rows is fast; the model is loaded once, not per event |
| Forecast budget | A counting-table lookup (well under 1 second) plus the polling delay |
| Containment budget | One state change plus the polling delay |
| Polling cost | An unchanged poll returns a tiny reply, so 2 to 4 clients polling every 1 to 2 seconds is light |
| NIDS reads | Each NIDS request reads the whole packet table; keeping it near 500 rows keeps this cheap |
| 3D console | A small graph keeps it smooth on modest laptops; tested early on the weakest laptop |
| Measurement | The integration test records timestamps at each stage so budgets are checked, not guessed |

