## 18. Error Handling and Fallbacks

### 18.1 Configuration Switches

| Variable | Values | Effect |
|---|---|---|
| `DATA_MODE` | `sample` or `live` | `sample` serves the contract sample files; `live` runs the real pipeline |
| `DETECTOR_MODE` | `nids` or `scripted` | `scripted` takes labels from the scenario file if NIDS's detector cannot run |
| `FORECAST_SOURCE` | `repo` or `lookup` | `lookup` uses the rule-based ATT&CK table |
| `REPLAY_SPEED` | Number | Speed factor |
| `DATABASE_URL` | Database address | SQLite by default |

### 18.2 Failure Table

| Failure | Behaviour |
|---|---|
| NIDS's detector cannot be called in-process | Switch to `DETECTOR_MODE=scripted`; log it; the pipeline continues |
| SQLite does not work with NIDS | Fall back to Docker Compose as NIDS ships it (documented fallback, heavier) |
| NIDS's pinned libraries do not run on the chosen Python | Use the Python version NIDS targets (3.9) for the backend environment, with separate environments for the other tools |
| Precog export fails | Switch to `FORECAST_SOURCE=lookup` |
| A scenario file is invalid | Reject it with a clear error and keep the previous state |
| Polling fails | Clients show stale state and retry |
| Push unavailable | Alerts still appear in the in-app feed |
| Hosted backend is asleep or down | Demo on localhost; or play the recorded video |
| Confirmation expires | Action becomes `expired`; nothing changes |
| A forecast cannot be produced | Show "no forecast available" |

