### 23.2 Glossary Additions

| Term | Meaning |
|---|---|
| **Add-on** | A file of our own that plugs extra routes or logic into the NIDS app without editing NIDS's files |
| **Blueprint** | Flask's way of grouping extra routes and registering them in one line |
| **Polling** | A client asking the server for updates at a regular interval |
| **Version number** | A counter that goes up on every state change, so a poll can say "nothing new" cheaply |
| **Feasible path** | A route between hosts that the topology and vulnerability data say an attacker could use |
| **Strategy profile** | One style of scripted attacker behaviour used to vary generated sequences |
| **Service worker** | A browser background script that makes a web app installable and able to show push notifications |
| **Virtual environment** | A private folder of Python packages for one piece of the project |
| **Placeholder file** | A starter file created first by LEAD-CORE that its owner later replaces |

